// Synthetic rows for the retrieval replay (tests/component/retrieval_replay):
// three ledgers, each with a measure per month whose doc runs to about 900
// characters, so the cards of one answer to "total amount" do not fit one
// 35,000-character page together and the answer is paged by size.

#(doc) One row per entry posted to the north ledger.
source: north_ledger is duckdb.sql("""
  select 1 as entry_id, 1 as posted_month, 100.0 as amount union all select 2, 2, 250.0
""") extend {
  primary_key: entry_id
  #(doc) Total amount posted to the north ledger in January, in US dollars before tax. Rule 1: an entry dated in January counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 2: an entry dated in January counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 3: an entry dated in January counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 4: an entry dated in January counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 5: an entry dated in January counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 6: an entry dated in January counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 7: an entry dated in January counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit.
  measure: total_amount_january is amount.sum() { where: posted_month = 1 }
  #(doc) Total amount posted to the north ledger in February, in US dollars before tax. Rule 1: an entry dated in February counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 2: an entry dated in February counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 3: an entry dated in February counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 4: an entry dated in February counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 5: an entry dated in February counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 6: an entry dated in February counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 7: an entry dated in February counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit.
  measure: total_amount_february is amount.sum() { where: posted_month = 2 }
  #(doc) Total amount posted to the north ledger in March, in US dollars before tax. Rule 1: an entry dated in March counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 2: an entry dated in March counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 3: an entry dated in March counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 4: an entry dated in March counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 5: an entry dated in March counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 6: an entry dated in March counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 7: an entry dated in March counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit.
  measure: total_amount_march is amount.sum() { where: posted_month = 3 }
  #(doc) Total amount posted to the north ledger in April, in US dollars before tax. Rule 1: an entry dated in April counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 2: an entry dated in April counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 3: an entry dated in April counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 4: an entry dated in April counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 5: an entry dated in April counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 6: an entry dated in April counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 7: an entry dated in April counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit.
  measure: total_amount_april is amount.sum() { where: posted_month = 4 }
  #(doc) Total amount posted to the north ledger in May, in US dollars before tax. Rule 1: an entry dated in May counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 2: an entry dated in May counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 3: an entry dated in May counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 4: an entry dated in May counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 5: an entry dated in May counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 6: an entry dated in May counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 7: an entry dated in May counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit.
  measure: total_amount_may is amount.sum() { where: posted_month = 5 }
  #(doc) Total amount posted to the north ledger in June, in US dollars before tax. Rule 1: an entry dated in June counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 2: an entry dated in June counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 3: an entry dated in June counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 4: an entry dated in June counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 5: an entry dated in June counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 6: an entry dated in June counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit. Rule 7: an entry dated in June counts here even when it was keyed in later, and a correction is a new entry, never an edit.
